{"availability":"available","full":"countervolts/d4r","name":"d4r","description":"NVIDIA's official DLSS 3/4/4.5 on AMD RDNA3/4 GPUs on Windows and Linux.","category":"Other","language":"C++","stars":268,"forks":9,"created":"2026-09-27T19:23:59Z","updated":"2026-10-10T21:58:22Z","license":"GPL-3.0","branch":"linux","homepage":"","topics":["amd","dlss","hip","linux","linux-gaming","optiscaler","proton","radeon","rdna3","rocm","wine","zluda"],"demo":"https://cdn.ayois.gay/dlss","color":"#302e55","ink":"#dbd2ff","lastCheckedAt":"2026-10-11T04:29:40.073Z","lastAttemptAt":"2026-10-11T04:29:40.073Z","lastAvailableAt":"2026-10-11T04:29:40.073Z","metrics":[{"at":"2026-10-11T04:29:40.073Z","stars":268,"forks":9}],"technologies":[],"overview":{"kind":"readme","version":1,"paragraphs":["d4r runs NVIDIA's official DLSS Super Resolution library (nvngxdlss.dll) in Windows games on AMD Radeon GPUs under Linux and Proton. The game asks for DLSS as usual; the DLSS network runs on the AMD GPU through ZLUDA (CUDA on ROCm/HIP), with the heaviest DLSS kernels replaced by hand-written RDNA3 and RDNA4 code.","Supported DLSS models: DLSS 3 CNN (E), DLSS 4 transformer (K, default), and DLSS 4.5 transformer (M, plus experimental L). DLSS 5 is PURPOSELY not supported.","Preset L is NVIDIA's DLSS 4.5 model for Ultra Performance, especially at 4K. Set [DLSS] Model = L in d4r.ini and select Ultra Performance in game or OptiScaler; selecting L alone does not change the input resolution. L shares M's native Swin layers and has its own texture-kernel build. Its unfolded input/output arithmetic remains translated, so performance and image quality need game testing; the M benchmarks below do not apply to L."],"features":[],"sourceUrl":"https://github.com/countervolts/d4r/blob/linux/README.md","fingerprint":"eab777d2856d6b436dee7dd1625f26e11052023068b2c4b04281ba06026b2711","extractedAt":"2026-10-11T04:29:40.278Z"},"overviewCheckedAt":"2026-10-11T04:29:40.278Z","projectInsights":{"version":1,"whatItDoe